WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.529
Speaker 1: So I have an admission to make
that might strike you as a weird thing for

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:10.540
someone who hosts a show about American politics
to say, I absolutely hate politics, I hate

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.540
it.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.370
And what I mean by that is not that I don't
care about the issues that I talk about on

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.370
the show.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.070
I care deeply about the issues that I address
on the show.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:25.660
What I mean is I hate the fact that the reason
the show is the way it is and that elections

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.800
are the way they are and that the country
is the way that that it is.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.970
And the political system we have is the one
we have is based on a huge portion of this

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:40.260
country being a combination of ignorant, bad
faith actors and people whose views are completely

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.100
retrograde and antithetical, immorally antithetical
to the direction that we as a country and

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.870
as a human race should be going.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:52.070
I hate that this is what politics is in the
United States.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.660
I don't like the fact that when I take phone
calls from the audience, part of what I have

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.710
to do, because the alternative is to allow
it to go unchallenged.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.710
I hate that.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:08.180
Part of what I have to do is talk to people
with just terrible, ignorant, disgusting ideas

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.020
rooted in misunderstandings of how the world
works and a backwards morality that I find

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.340
to be despicable, to put it, to put it lightly.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.970
I don't want to have people like that in my
life.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.650
It's optional that such people exist.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.040
It doesn't have to be this way.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:29.010
We could have a more informed and educated
population, but this is what it is.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:35.270
And I hate the fact that this is what it means
to engage in politics in the United States.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.560
It's dealing with these horrible people and
bad ideas.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:45.110
I hate that because of these reactionary right
wing movements, when we have a pandemic, we

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.380
actually have to fight people just to get
them to accept uncontroversial science.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.790
It's a waste of time, but it has to be done
because it's what we're dealing with.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.770
I hate that when we could be figuring out,
I don't know how to move away from dirty energy

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.960
and start treating the planet with some respect
and reorganizing our economies and societies

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.940
to be more sustainable, we're still dealing
with people who just don't accept the science.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.060
We're still dealing with people who, you know,
they don't think abortion should be legal

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.560
or that two gay people should be able to legally
get married.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.560
It's disgusting.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.590
It's a waste of time.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.320
Look at what we have to deal with because
of how things work in the United States.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.060
And one of the real frustrations of American
politics is that much like some aspects of

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.200
consumer culture, we're wasting time thinking
about the wrong things.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:38.590
What I mean by that is I recently watched
some great interviews with the late author

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.940
David Foster Wallace, whose book Infinite
Jest I'm reading now.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:49.380
And one of the things that struck me about
his sort of critique of consumer culture and

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:55.220
even David Foster Wallace critique of much
of the kind of literary analysis space is

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:01.630
that we spend very little time actually thinking
about are we thinking about the right things?

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:08.250
And when we look at the points of focus for
American politics and media is the reality

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:14.340
that these are the things we focus on because
there are people that are so ignorant and

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.170
reactionary that they want to fight us on
them.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:23.270
You then start to realize how much we're really
missing in our ability to make progress.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:28.640
And I'll give you some examples here in the
United States, the modern political media

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.760
space ends up saying very little about what
are some of the biggest questions of our time

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.760
right now?

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:43.920
Are we, as a human race, advanced enough and
wealthy enough to end abject poverty and that

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.230
degree of human suffering and make sure everybody
is at least housed and fed?

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.800
This is a really fundamental and basic question.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.170
And the answer is obviously, yes, it's a matter
of political will.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.940
We should just be figuring out, hey, you know
what?

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.270
We've got the money and we've got the Know-How.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.760
Let's end abject poverty.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.459
Let's end global hunger.

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:07.350
But it becomes completely intractable because
we have to deal with people who immediately

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:13.720
go to socialist this and communist that and
Trumpy and free markets and supply side economics.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.690
I mean, trash, truly trash.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:21.630
Another question, are we going to figure out
a way to organize ourselves so that we.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:27.060
And live what I would call sustainably on
this planet, we can do it, it's a matter of

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.020
how we do it, not whether we need to.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:36.540
And we are rapidly advancing in so many technologies
solar, electric vehicles, geothermal, carbon

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.730
capture.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:43.780
But instead of having a society that is doing
really an incredibly patriotic or humanistic

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:49.090
thing and saying we are dealing with this
right now, we're all together furthering this

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:52.841
technology and we're on the same page that
we just have to do this for the sake of the

00:04:52.841 --> 00:04:53.841
human race.

00:04:53.841 --> 00:04:56.730
We've identified the problem and we're dealing
with it now.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:02.231
Instead, we're relegated to arguing with people
who won't even accept it's a problem, who

00:05:02.231 --> 00:05:09.240
think it makes a scientific point to bring
a snowball inside indoors in Washington, D.C.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.600
in winter.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.180
It's just a total garbage situation.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:20.020
And so what I mean when I say I seriously
hate politics is that I hate that this is

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:23.550
what we have to deal with when we engage with
the political system.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:28.290
Now, obviously, to change the system, you
have to engage with it.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:34.510
If you just ignore the system, bury your head
in the sand, you accomplish nothing other

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:38.900
than letting the people with the worst instincts
make all the decisions.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.990
That's tragic and that's devastating.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:46.460
And so in order to fix American politics,
we do have to pay attention and we do have

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:51.419
to engage with these retrograde, disgusting,
baseless ideas.

00:05:51.419 --> 00:06:19.300
And that's what I mean by hating politics,
because we have to face the reality t

